  lib_common/sound_link.vhd       FPGA -> ESP32 telemetry UART (sound events,
                                  game/family, ball, link health, RAM snapshots).
  lib_common/disp_inject.vhd      ESP32 -> FPGA one-wire control/display UART,
                                  with fail-safe timeouts.
  lib_common/ram_snoop.vhd        read-only RIOT + 5101 RAM shadow/streamer.
  lib_common/ta_overlay.vhd       time-attack countdown painted into ONE display
                                  of the running multiplex.
  lib_common/tourney_block.vhd    solenoid masking hook for tournament mode
                                  (currently a no-op placeholder).
  lib_common/ay_3_8910.vhd        AY-3-8910 PSG core (written, NOT instantiated).
  lib_common/tourney_countdown.vhd, value_to_dispstr.vhd, bin_to_bcd.vhd,
  tourney_display_top.vhd         FPGA-side countdown chain, superseded by the
                                  ESP-side implementation (NOT instantiated).
  sim/*                           GHDL testbenches and the regression runner.
  GottFA80_PLuS_HW21x_Cyclone_10/build.sh
                                  reproducible build + manifest generator.

MODIFIED UPSTREAM FILES

  GottFA80_PLuS_HW21x_Cyclone_10/SYS80.vhd
      - game ROM sourced from nor_flash instead of SD_Card
      - shared-SPI arbitration and I/O mux for diagnostic mode; ESP bus grant
      - System 80/80A/80B family decode replaces the unsound strobe-counting
        auto-detect and the hard-wired `not80B <= '1'`
      - 80B gate on the display mux so the numeric banner is not pushed into an
        alphanumeric glass
      - sound bus reported as strobe-qualified EVENTS to the ESP
      - time-attack: auto-restart by synthetic switch closures, end-on-demand
        via a slam pulse, countdown overlay
      - RAM snapshot streamer; link telemetry
      - LED_Int repurposed to the attract/game detector
  GottFA80_PLuS_HW21x_Cyclone_10/SYS80.qsf
      - new source files; Audio_RX (PIN_2) turned into a pulled-up input
  GottFA80_PLuS_HW21x_Cyclone_10/SYS80.sdc
      - the generated CPU clock and two documented, narrowly scoped false paths
  lib_common/boot_message.vhd     four display strings instead of a fixed banner
  lib_common/detect_sw.vhd        long-press detection (diag entry); stuck-pulse fix
  lib_common/SN7448_GTB.vhd       glyph additions for the overlay
  lib_common/GOSOF80.vhd          diagnostic sound injection hook
  lib_common/R6532.vhd            port-A write strobe exported for snd_bus
